Set errno when connect or bind fails.
The connect and bind wrappers returned the Winsock failure without
copying WSAGetLastError() into errno, as the sendto and recv wrappers
do. Callers report errno, so the message showed whatever an earlier
call had left there: "nc HOST http" to a closed port said "can't connect
to remote host (HOST): Invalid argument", left over from parsing the
service name as a number, a numeric port gave no reason at all, and
"nc -l -p PORT" on a port in use said just "bind". Set errno from the
Winsock error so the real cause is reported.

---
 win32/net.c |   10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/win32/net.c
+++ b/win32/net.c
@@ -132,14 +132,20 @@
 int FAST_FUNC mingw_connect(int sockfd, const struct sockaddr *sa, size_t sz)
 {
 	SOCKET s = (SOCKET)_get_osfhandle(sockfd);
-	return connect(s, sa, sz);
+	int res = connect(s, sa, sz);
+	if (res < 0)
+		errno = WSAGetLastError();
+	return res;
 }
 
 #undef bind
 int FAST_FUNC mingw_bind(int sockfd, struct sockaddr *sa, size_t sz)
 {
 	SOCKET s = (SOCKET)_get_osfhandle(sockfd);
-	return bind(s, sa, sz);
+	int res = bind(s, sa, sz);
+	if (res < 0)
+		errno = WSAGetLastError();
+	return res;
 }
 
 #undef sendto
